// BDE -> FireDAC conversion library -- a STARTING POINT, not a finished rule book.
//
// Assembled 2026-08-02 from convrules\FireDAC_Migrate_BDE.rules (Embarcadero's
// reFind corpus, imported verbatim and NOT modified). That corpus is 60 flat
// #migrate lines; this file re-expresses the part of it the ConvRules editor can
// work with -- one #convert block per component pair, with the property links
// filled in -- and carries the rest through unchanged at the bottom.
//
// WHAT IS CORPUS-SUPPLIED (trust it): every #unuse and #remove line, the units on
//   each #convert header, both #mapping blocks, and the #link lines under a
//   '#note corpus' marker. These come from Embarcadero's own migration rules.
//
// WHAT IS MACHINE-GENERATED (review it): the #link lines under a
//   '#note auto-matched' marker. They were produced by the editor's own Auto-Match
//   rule, replayed headlessly against `drag-lint proptree --min-visibility
//   published --refs-as-leaves` for both sides (library-Win64 index): a source
//   leaf is paired only when exactly ONE writable, still-unassigned target leaf
//   has the same FULL PATH and a legal cast; failing that, only when the source
//   leaf's NAME is unique among ALL target last-segments and exactly one such
//   target is castable. Nothing ambiguous was guessed.
//
// WHAT STILL NEEDS A HUMAN:
//   * Every block's '#note outstanding:' line counts the source properties that
//     got NO target. They were deliberately left out rather than invented.
//   * The #migrate lines at the bottom could not become property links -- they
//     rename METHODS (Session.*, FindDatabase, AddAlias, TDatabase:Execute), or
//     enum types with no property that carries them (TUpdateKind, TUpdateAction,
//     TDBScreenCursors), or classes with no published surface at all
//     (TBlobStream, EDBEngineError). They are carried VERBATIM, not dropped.
//   * convert-apply does not evaluate #mapping/#apply yet (DSL doc, Known limits
//     #1), so a post-save `convert-validate` reports those two directives as
//     unknown. The file is correct; the engine has not caught up.
//
// Unit/file renames (uAD.inc -> FireDAC.inc and 210 more) are a DIFFERENT domain
// and are deliberately NOT merged here -- see convrules\FireDAC_Rename_Units.rules.
//
// Plain 7-bit ASCII, CRLF.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 1. BDE units to drop (corpus, verbatim)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#unuse BDE.DBTables
#unuse BDE.BDEConst
#unuse DBTables
#unuse BDEConst
#unuse BDEMTS
#unuse BDE

// Corpus, verbatim: properties with no FireDAC counterpart at all.
#remove SessionName
#remove PrivateDir
#remove DFM: Origin

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 2. Enum-valued property conversions (corpus). Only the two groups that a
//    #convert block below actually consumes are expressed as #mapping; the
//    other three enum groups have no property carrying them and stay #migrate.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#mapping BdeTransIsolation from Bde.DBTables.TTransIsolation to FireDAC.Comp.Client.TFDConnection
#mapping BdeTransIsolation #when TransIsolation = tiDirtyRead -> TxOptions.Isolation = xiDirtyRead
#mapping BdeTransIsolation #when TransIsolation = tiReadCommitted -> TxOptions.Isolation = xiReadCommitted
#mapping BdeTransIsolation #when TransIsolation = tiRepeatableRead -> TxOptions.Isolation = xiRepeatableRead

#mapping BdeBatchMode from Bde.DBTables.TBatchMode to FireDAC.Comp.BatchMove.TFDBatchMove
#mapping BdeBatchMode #when Mode = batAppend -> Mode = dmAppend
#mapping BdeBatchMode #when Mode = batUpdate -> Mode = dmUpdate
#mapping BdeBatchMode #when Mode = batAppendUpdate -> Mode = dmAppendUpdate
#mapping BdeBatchMode #when Mode = batDelete -> Mode = dmDelete
#mapping BdeBatchMode #when Mode = batCopy -> Mode = dmAlwaysInsert

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 3. Component conversions
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

